# {{.AppName}}

A production-ready Go HTTP server, generated with [GoForge](https://github.com/Frank5ive/goforge).

## Features

- `GET /health` endpoint returning JSON
- Graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM (in-flight requests get 30 seconds to finish)
- Request IDs (`X-Request-ID`) and panic recovery middleware
- HTTP timeouts, including `ReadHeaderTimeout` against slow-header attacks{{if .IncludeLogger}}
- Structured logging with `log/slog` (text or JSON) and per-request logs{{end}}
- Tests, a Makefile, and a golangci-lint config{{if .IncludeDocker}}
- Multi-stage Dockerfile running as a non-root user, with a health check{{end}}{{if .IncludeCI}}
- GitHub Actions CI: vet, race-enabled tests, and lint{{if .IncludeDocker}}, plus a Docker build{{end}}{{end}}

## Requirements

- Go 1.24 or newer{{if .IncludeDocker}}
- Docker (optional){{end}}

## Getting started

```bash
make run          # or: go run .
curl http://localhost:{{.Port}}/health
```

Run `make help` to see all commands:

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `make run` | Run the server |
| `make build` | Build the binary into `bin/` |
| `make test` | Run tests |
| `make cover` | Run tests and open the coverage report |
| `make lint` | Run `go vet` and [golangci-lint](https://golangci-lint.run) |
| `make fmt` | Format code |{{if .IncludeDocker}}
| `make docker-build` | Build the Docker image |
| `make docker-run` | Run the Docker image on port {{.Port}} |{{end}}

## Configuration

Configuration comes from environment variables:

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `PORT` | Port the server listens on | `{{.Port}}` |
| `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API from a browser, or `*` | CORS disabled |
| `MAX_BODY_BYTES` | Maximum request body size; larger bodies get `413` | `1048576` (1 MiB) |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | How long in-flight requests get to finish on shutdown | `30s` |{{if .IncludeLogger}}
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug`, `info`, `warn`, or `error` | `info` |
| `LOG_FORMAT` | `text` or `json` (use `json` in production) | `text` |{{end}}

## API

### `GET /health`

Reports that the service is up.

```bash
curl http://localhost:{{.Port}}/health
```

```json
{
  "status": "healthy",
  "timestamp": "2026-01-01T12:00:00Z",
  "service": "{{.AppName}}"
}
```

### `GET /readyz`

Reports whether the service can handle traffic: `200 {"status":"ready"}`, or `503` when a
dependency such as the database is unavailable. Point load balancer and Kubernetes
readiness probes here, and liveness probes at `/health`.

Every response includes an `X-Request-ID` header. Send your own `X-Request-ID` to
trace a request across services; otherwise one is generated.

